deps-restorer: replace a hoisted package by renaming the old tree aside on every kernel (homescoop#1384)

0010 kept upstream's remove-then-rename where the host says directory renames
aren't cheap (slicc-kernel < 1.134.3). That path deletes the old tree file by
file before the new one goes in, and a delete that fails partway (an entry
pnpm can't unlink, such as a file in a read-only directory) left the package
gutted: the deleted files were gone, and only node_modules/ was restored.
Now every kernel renames the old tree aside, renames the staged one in, and
puts the old tree back if that fails. On older kernels the rename copies the
tree, which is slower but leaves the old package whole if anything fails.

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).

